            0.081
          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 6"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.119,
            0.885,
            0.163
          ],
          "content": "One way is to visualise the final figure by drawing a rough diagram of it."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.388,
            0.171,
            0.676,
            0.315
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_13_image_2.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.34,
            0.593,
            0.361
          ],
          "content": "What can we infer from this figure?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.366,
            0.564,
            0.388
          ],
          "content": "Can you identify the equal sides?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.393,
            0.593,
            0.415
          ],
          "content": "Since, the two squares are identical,"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.42,
            0.43,
            0.441
          ],
          "content": "AB = BC and FE = ED"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.446,
            0.884,
            0.491
          ],
          "content": "Since ABEF and BCDE are squares, all the sides in each of the squares are equal. This is written as —"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.495,
            0.401,
            0.516
          ],
          "content": "AF = AB = BE = FE"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.208,
            0.518,
            0.403,
            0.538
          ],
          "content": "BE = BC = CD = ED"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.545,
            0.572,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": "So, all the shorter lines are equal!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.571,
            0.884,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "A convention is followed to represent equal sides. It is done by putting a ‘|’ on the line. Refer to the rough figure."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.621,
            0.885,
            0.688
          ],
          "content": "Using this analysis, can you try constructing it? Remember, all that was asked for is a rectangle that can be divided into two identical squares and with no measurements imposed."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.689,
            0.885,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": "To draw the rectangle ACDF, one could assign any length to AF. For example, if we assign AF = 4 cm, then what must the length of AC be?"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.753,
            0.735,
            0.776
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Explore: Can the rectangle now be completed?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.789,
            0.886,
            0.88
          ],
          "content": "In fact, one could proceed by drawing AF without even measuring its length using a ruler. We could then construct a line perpendicular to AF that is long enough to contain the other side. As, AB = AF, we need to somehow transfer the length of AF"
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "bbox": [
            0.082,
            0.941,
            0.117,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": ""
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
          "bbox": [
            0.449,
            0.97,
            0.55,
            0.986
          ],
          "content": "Reprint 2026-27"
        }
      ]
    }
